# Server logs from a run are useful while you are looking at a result
# and are not part of it. The raw k6 samples, the summary and the
# hardware stanza are the artifact, and those are committed.
*.log

# Best effort resident memory samples from a soak. Keep one by force
# (git add -f) when it is the evidence for a leak; otherwise it is
# noise, and on platforms where sampling did not work it is a column
# of "unknown".
*.rss.csv
